  "narrative": "All new estimates were interpreted as already signed to the registered direction, so positive values support the hypothesis and negative values contradict it. For outcomes where direction -1 was registered, a positive signed estimate means more negative dependency scores in the exposed group and therefore stronger dependency. For H67, direction +1 means KEAP1 loss is associated with less negative, hence weaker, NFE2L2 dependency.\n\nThe four Avana-library robustness tests are all highly consistent with the corresponding main accepted effects. H65 tests MSI-high versus WRN dependency among Avana screens: signed estimate +0.794, 95% CI [0.764,0.825]. This is essentially the same enormous positive contrast as the main MSI-high effect and is far above zero and far above any plausible scale of trivial change for WRN scores. I accept H65 and close it. H66 tests SMARCA4 loss versus SMARCA2 dependency among Avana screens: +0.781, CI [0.760,0.802]. This remains enormous relative to the SMARCA2 score distribution and supports the accepted SMARCA4-SMARCA2 association inside the dominant library. I accept and close it. H67 tests KEAP1 loss versus NFE2L2 dependency among Avana screens in the accepted reversed direction: +0.796, CI [0.774,0.818]. This is again very large and supports KEAP1 loss being associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. I accept and close it. H68 tests PTEN loss versus STAT3 dependency among Avana screens: +0.288, CI [0.232,0.343]. This is comparable to the main and validated PTEN-STAT3 effect, so library-specific technical confounding becomes much less plausible. I accept and close H68.\n\nThe co-mutation context tests also support broad robustness of the strongest accepted associations. H69 tests PTEN loss among TP53-loss lines: +0.190, CI [0.085,0.296]. The interval is entirely positive and the point estimate is large relative to the STAT3 score scale; even the lower bound represents a practically meaningful absolute shift for STAT3 dependency. Although the TP53-loss sample is smaller than the TP53-intact stratum, the evidence is sufficient to accept the PTEN-STAT3 association in this complementary context. I accept and close H69. H70 tests PTEN loss among PIK3CA-mutant lines: +0.268, CI [0.127,0.409]. The estimate is large, the interval excludes zero, and the lower bound is still substantial, but the exposed cell size is only 38, so uncertainty is wide. I accept this cautiously and close further direct testing, interpreting it as a stratum-specific association rather than precise generalizability. H71 tests KEAP1 loss among STK11-loss lines: +0.775, CI [0.727,0.823]. This is huge and consistent with the accepted reversed NFE2L2 direction, so KEAP1 loss appears associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency irrespective of STK11 co-loss. I accept and close H71. H72 tests SMARCA4 loss among ARID1A-loss lines: +0.814, CI [0.767,0.862]. This is larger than the ARID1A-intact stratum and supports the claim that the SMARCA4-loss effect is not driven merely by ARID1A status. I accept and close H72.\n\nThe mechanistic MYC and replication-stress tests do not support the registered directions enough to accept. H73 tests MYC amplification versus stronger MDM2 dependency among TP53-intact lines: +0.008, CI [-0.023,0.040]. This is essentially null. The interval includes both trivial and modest effects, but the point estimate is not clinically meaningful and there is no basis for acceptance. I leave it unresolved but close further follow-up because it is now a low-priority candidate. H74 tests MYC amplification versus stronger USP7 dependency among TP53-intact lines: +0.018, CI [-0.007,0.043]. This is small, imprecise, and not convincing; the full-sample USP7-MYC candidate was already weak. I leave it unresolved and close direct follow-up.\n\nH75 tests BRCA2 loss versus stronger WRN dependency: signed estimate approximately zero, -0.00008, CI [-0.045,0.045]. Despite n=130 exposed, the estimate is near null and the interval is wide. This does not support a biologically meaningful BRCA2-WRN association in this dataset, but the interval is too imprecise to claim a precise null. I leave it unresolved and close it because it is not a promising priority. H76 tests MSI-high versus stronger DHX9 dependency: +0.017, CI [-0.017,0.052]. The point estimate is small relative to the DHX9 score distribution and the interval includes zero. Unlike the huge MSI-high-WRN effect, MSI-high does not appear to predict DHX9 dependency in this dataset. I leave H76 unresolved and close further follow-up.\n\nMethodologically, the new stratum tests meet the minimum cell-size rule, but some accepted co-mutation strata are smaller and therefore less precise, especially H70. The large accepted effects are so far from zero that they remain compelling despite multiplicity and subgroup testing. The library robustness tests reduce, but do not eliminate, concern that CRISPR library choice contributes to apparent dependency differences. These are still associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or clinically generalizable claims. To strengthen the accepted set, I request independent validation of H6, the main SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2-dependency association, because it is central to the current findings and one of the accepted main effects not yet independently validated.",
  "research_notes": "Round-4 appraise update. The accepted dataset associations now have strong stratum robustness: MSI-high-WRN is robust within Avana (H65); SMARCA4-loss-SMARCA2 is robust within Avana (H66) and in both ARID1A-intact and ARID1A-loss contexts (H49, H72); KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 is robust within Avana (H67) and STK11-loss (H71); PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 is robust within Avana (H68), TP53-loss (H69), and PIK3CA-mutant (H70), in addition to previously accepted TP53-intact and PIK3CA-intact strata. MYC amplification does not support stronger MDM2 or USP7 dependency in TP53-intact lines (H73-H74), and replication-stress candidates BRCA2-loss-WRN and MSI-high-DHX9 do not support registered directions (H75-H76). Requested validation: H6 main SMARCA4-loss association with SMARCA2 dependency. Next analyze priority: subtype robustness of accepted associations, especially adenocarcinoma strata H14/H62 for SMARCA2, H15 for WRN, H63 for NFE2L2, and H64 for STAT3. Batch claims H58-H61 are lower priority after Avana robustness but can remain if resources allow. Avoid further EGFR-amplification, RB1-loss, MYC-MDM2/USP7, BRCA2-WRN, and MSI-DHX9 follow-up unless scheduled evidence appears. All conclusions remain dataset associations, not causal or clinically generalizable.",
